{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"0781419b7dbad767f9b8a73378e3abd74dd74f22d865fbb8284a76d9c5878171","digest":{"component_or_area":"snapshot janitor / cache reclamation","key_entities":["docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md","src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/cache.py","src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py","_gc_pass","materialize_tickets","add_bytes","byte_total","max_bytes","free_watermark_bytes","startup_sweep","_is_entry","REBAR_GATE_MAX_BYTES","tests/unit/test_snapshot_janitor.py"],"problem_keywords":["snapshot cache","garbage collection","byte accounting","disk reclamation","unimplemented trigger"],"propositions":["The ADR-promised byte-total backstop trigger in _gc_pass was never implemented; _gc_pass reads only free-space and mtime, never consulting the incrementally-maintained byte_total counter.","materialize_tickets populates tickets-<sha> entries (~620 MiB each, the store's dominant consumers) without calling add_bytes, leaving them invisible to the byte-accounting ledger.","The snapshot store has no size-based reclaim mechanism at all due to the missing backstop, and no configurable cap knob exists in the config surface.","With the byte-total trigger unimplemented and materialize_tickets unaccounted, the store breached 90% disk usage with no eviction, despite GC infrastructure being wired and runnable."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787360405576763163,"uuid":"4e32e2d3-4c28-4b08-85e5-f95a5b39c629"}